 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Self-Intersection (Acne):** Floating-point precision errors can cause the sample point to be slightly inside the geometry, resulting in negative distances and incorrect occlusion. A small bias offset along the normal is required [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** The accuracy of the AO depends on the resolution of the SDF. Low-resolution SDFs may produce blocky or inaccurate occlusion.
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** At the boundaries of the SDF grid, queries may return undefined or large values. Proper handling of grid boundaries is necessary [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Parameter Tuning:** The scale, decay, and number of samples significantly affect the visual result. Too few samples may result in noisy or inaccurate AO, while too many may be computationally expensive [S2, S3, S4, unofficial].
